; G14 pointer builtins — read path. HIR channel parity.
; Semantics under test:
;   - `&x` yields a pointer whose element type mirrors the variable's type
;   - `load(px)` decodes the pointed-to value through that element type
; Scope: scalar I64 only. This fixture exercises the read path alone, so a
; `pointerLoad` regression cannot be masked by a `pointerStore` one. The
; snapshot-versus-reference split is deliberately not exercised — see the
; sibling `testDiffPointerStore` for why.

main|func() -> ():
    var x: I64 = 7
    var px = unsafe &x
    print(unsafe load(px))
    return
